The Rendering Engine: MuPDFTo handle complex document formats (PDF, EPUB, XPS) without the overhead of a desktop environment, Akshara-Pi utilizes the MuPDF C-library. This allows for high-fidelity vector-to-bitmap conversion while maintaining the "Literata" typography standards.⚙️ Why MuPDF for Pi Zero 2 W?Low Memory Footprint: It typically operates within 15MB–25MB of RAM, leaving plenty of overhead for the Pi's 512MB total capacity.Superior Anti-Aliasing: It produces high-quality grayscale bitmaps that translate perfectly to E-ink’s 16-level grayscale capabilities.Multi-Format Support: A single library handles both fixed-layout (PDF) and reflowable (EPUB) text.🛠️ Technical Integration (The C-Logic)In the Akshara-Pi source code, the integration follows a "Request-Render-Release" lifecycle to prevent memory leaks:Context Creation: Initialize the fz_context to manage global resources.Document Loading: Open the file from the /books directory into an fz_document object.Page Mapping: Scale the document page to fit the $600 \times 448$ (or your 5.76" display's specific) resolution.Rasterization: Draw the page into an fz_pixmap.Bitmap Conversion: Extract the raw pixel data from the pixmap and pass it to the E-ink's SPI buffer.
